      "summaryOfTheGaps": "The good news is you are not starting from scratch. Strengths like Data Analysis, Problem-Solving, and Attention to Detail carry straight over and give you a real head start. What is newer is the craft at the center of it, things like Vision Formation, Requirements Management, and User Stories. You will also grow into the everyday work, like Requirements Gathering and Requirements Refinement. Just as important is how the work happens on a team. Practices like Shared Ownership, Empowerment, and Shared Leadership are less about tools and more about how you show up with the people around you. You will not learn all of this up front. Like the work itself, you grow into it a piece at a time, taking on a little more as you go.",
